1
00:00:05,791 --> 00:00:07,468
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,493 --> 00:00:09,140
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:10,952 --> 00:00:12,932
(Episode 17)

4
00:00:17,726 --> 00:00:21,595
This isn't the way to our house.

5
00:00:25,902 --> 00:00:27,442
Where are we going?

6
00:00:28,103 --> 00:00:29,308
Gyeol.

7
00:00:31,735 --> 00:00:33,474
Want to go somewhere...

8
00:00:34,435 --> 00:00:38,055
where no one knows us and live there?
Just you, your mom, and me.

9
00:01:10,741 --> 00:01:12,430
Do you know where this is?

10
00:01:20,268 --> 00:01:22,690
Really? Amazing.

11
00:01:23,388 --> 00:01:25,963
My friend says he hardly ever
uses this place,

12
00:01:26,922 --> 00:01:29,227
so we're welcome
to come here anytime we want.

13
00:01:32,521 --> 00:01:35,734
I've never seen a house this pretty.

14
00:01:39,495 --> 00:01:41,114
Should I just buy this place?

15
00:01:42,206 --> 00:01:46,038
That's it.
I'll tell him we're signing tomorrow.

16
00:01:46,655 --> 00:01:48,699
I can't say anything around you.

17
00:01:48,724 --> 00:01:50,719
You'd buy me anything I mention.

18
00:01:51,442 --> 00:01:55,359
Anything you want, I'll do for you.
I'll buy you anything you like.

19
00:01:55,694 --> 00:01:58,296
What else? The stars?

20
00:01:59,562 --> 00:02:01,079
The stars will have to wait.

21
00:02:02,841 --> 00:02:04,962
They haven't been listed yet.

22
00:02:07,315 --> 00:02:09,597
You're impossible.

23
00:02:10,629 --> 00:02:12,239
I better not say anything anymore.

24
00:02:13,374 --> 00:02:15,534
What do I do with you?

25
00:02:16,982 --> 00:02:19,128
How are you this lovable?

26
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:24,113
I want to hide you away
and keep you to myself.

27
00:02:26,128 --> 00:02:28,633
How did you get so much on your face?

28
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:31,577
You've got plenty on yours too.

29
00:02:31,608 --> 00:02:33,404
- I do?
- Come here.

30
00:02:40,018 --> 00:02:41,412
Good, right?

31
00:02:56,808 --> 00:03:00,518
I bought this house from him.

32
00:03:08,415 --> 00:03:12,722
Gyeol will wake up wondering where he is.
He'll be so surprised.

33
00:03:14,875 --> 00:03:18,290
- Are you hungry?
- No, I'm fine.

34
00:03:18,762 --> 00:03:21,084
Let me see what's in the fridge first.

35
00:03:26,622 --> 00:03:28,150
Thank you for coming with me.

36
00:03:32,695 --> 00:03:37,269
If you'd said no, I'd have cried
out of embarrassment.

37
00:04:09,982 --> 00:04:11,458
Is pork belly all right?

38
00:04:11,685 --> 00:04:14,865
I found some aged kimchi
and pork belly in the fridge.

39
00:04:15,625 --> 00:04:17,035
Give me that. I'll do it.

40
00:04:17,895 --> 00:04:19,970
Don't lift a finger. Just sit.

41
00:04:22,835 --> 00:04:24,776
Should I wake Gyeol up to eat?

42
00:04:25,862 --> 00:04:27,202
Let's let him sleep.

43
00:04:27,379 --> 00:04:28,794
He must have been exhausted.

44
00:04:29,942 --> 00:04:31,507
Right, that's better.

45
00:04:33,148 --> 00:04:35,279
I'll just cook again when he's up.

46
00:04:47,929 --> 00:04:51,584
This house hasn't changed at all.

47
00:04:51,775 --> 00:04:54,074
Because I left everything just as it was.

48
00:04:56,495 --> 00:04:59,492
When you came back someday,
we could come here together.

49
00:05:00,322 --> 00:05:03,142
So, I kept everything just the way it was.

50
00:05:22,708 --> 00:05:23,902
- What?
- Han Gyu Seo.

51
00:05:23,934 --> 00:05:27,630
Gyu Rim still isn't home.
It's past eleven.

52
00:05:28,435 --> 00:05:29,890
She went on a trip with Gyeol.

53
00:05:30,268 --> 00:05:32,371
She texted me earlier,
telling me not to worry and go to sleep.

54
00:05:32,396 --> 00:05:33,458
Sorry, I didn't tell you.

55
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:36,919
A trip with Gyeol? Out of nowhere? Where?

56
00:05:37,562 --> 00:05:38,885
I don't know where.

57
00:05:40,489 --> 00:05:42,569
She probably went with Mu Jin.

58
00:05:44,101 --> 00:05:46,114
She went with him?

59
00:05:46,541 --> 00:05:48,913
Is Gyu Rim seeing Mu Jin again?

60
00:05:48,975 --> 00:05:50,150
Did they decide to get back together?

61
00:05:50,175 --> 00:05:53,402
Weren't you dead set against
them getting back together?

62
00:05:53,588 --> 00:05:56,034
That was
because I worried it'd be hard on her.

63
00:05:56,174 --> 00:05:58,951
I've liked Mu Jin from the very start.

64
00:05:59,757 --> 00:06:01,947
You have no idea
how hard it was to hide it.

65
00:06:01,972 --> 00:06:05,909
Right? If you'd kept fighting it,
I was going to take you with me,

66
00:06:05,962 --> 00:06:08,096
and we'd have joined a monastery.

67
00:06:08,188 --> 00:06:12,309
Han Gyu Rim, get out here! Right now!

68
00:06:12,741 --> 00:06:14,286
She still hasn't moved out?

69
00:06:14,508 --> 00:06:17,119
Get out here, Han Gyu Rim! Now!

70
00:06:22,055 --> 00:06:24,987
Just because you're a year older,
you think you can boss me around?

71
00:06:25,025 --> 00:06:27,387
Who are you to lecture me?

72
00:06:27,455 --> 00:06:29,662
You can't even handle your own life.

73
00:06:29,921 --> 00:06:35,172
You don't even know how blood types
are passed down, and you're giving advice?

74
00:06:35,624 --> 00:06:38,430
You're dumb, clueless, and ignorant.

75
00:06:38,995 --> 00:06:41,011
Get out here now, Han Gyu Rim!

76
00:06:44,095 --> 00:06:46,770
Hey, Han Gyu O! You get out here too.

77
00:06:46,868 --> 00:06:50,667
This punk treats his own sister like dirt.

78
00:06:50,692 --> 00:06:55,027
You only finished middle school. You dare
to talk back to me, who studied abroad?

79
00:06:55,241 --> 00:06:57,526
You can't even spell Christmas.

80
00:06:57,795 --> 00:06:59,968
Get out! Right now!

81
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,861
Come on, fight me, you punk!

82
00:07:05,488 --> 00:07:09,779
You guys, seriously? Scared?

83
00:07:10,455 --> 00:07:14,242
What did these blockheads learn from?

84
00:07:14,362 --> 00:07:16,951
Who taught you guys to act like...

85
00:07:21,252 --> 00:07:26,614
Right. You reap what you sow, don't you?

86
00:07:33,528 --> 00:07:36,767
The man who raised such terrible kids!

87
00:07:36,842 --> 00:07:42,118
The man named Han Seok Jung,
an embarrassment wherever he goes!

88
00:07:45,075 --> 00:07:47,573
Not one of you showed up,

89
00:07:47,598 --> 00:07:51,607
so I ate all that food and drank all
that expensive liquor by myself!

90
00:07:55,715 --> 00:07:58,002
I said it was the last time...

91
00:07:58,175 --> 00:08:00,855
I said we'd never see each other again...

92
00:08:02,742 --> 00:08:08,022
The man who goes crazy for meatballs,
why didn't you come? Why?

93
00:08:08,328 --> 00:08:11,981
What kind of father acts this petty?

94
00:08:12,006 --> 00:08:15,406
What kind of father does this?

95
00:08:29,515 --> 00:08:32,099
Open the door.

96
00:08:32,209 --> 00:08:35,420
Let's have a talk!

97
00:08:35,445 --> 00:08:38,457
Wash your feet and go to sleep.

98
00:08:44,895 --> 00:08:48,068
Stop your drunken antics before someone
reports you for the noise,

99
00:08:48,093 --> 00:08:51,040
and go inside and get some sleep.

100
00:08:51,065 --> 00:08:52,957
What is this now?

101
00:08:53,395 --> 00:08:55,369
It's not "this." It's Han Gyu Min.

102
00:08:55,515 --> 00:08:58,776
Han Gyu Min. Just the one I wanted.

103
00:08:59,183 --> 00:09:01,802
How dare you ignore my text?

104
00:09:01,902 --> 00:09:06,215
I treated you like human beings and asked
for one last meal together,

105
00:09:06,389 --> 00:09:08,209
and you ignored my message?

106
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:11,111
If I'd gone, you'd have screamed
about that too!

107
00:09:11,205 --> 00:09:13,145
And what? Treated us like humans?

108
00:09:13,468 --> 00:09:14,823
Are Gyu Seo and I insects, then?

109
00:09:14,848 --> 00:09:16,343
Are we sea anemones?

110
00:09:16,688 --> 00:09:19,312
How dare you talk back to your sister...

111
00:09:19,455 --> 00:09:21,915
What sister? You're no sister.

112
00:09:22,082 --> 00:09:24,035
When have you ever treated
Gyu Seo and me like siblings?

113
00:09:24,427 --> 00:09:27,669
To you we're the unteachables!

114
00:09:27,694 --> 00:09:30,048
Hey! You ignorant thing.

115
00:09:30,495 --> 00:09:34,522
It's not unteachables, it's untouchables.

116
00:09:34,628 --> 00:09:36,555
How embarrassing. So humiliating.

117
00:09:36,675 --> 00:09:39,776
Don't you dare tell anyone
you know me. I swear.

118
00:09:39,801 --> 00:09:42,772
Fine, I won't. Never.

119
00:09:42,797 --> 00:09:45,652
When friends ask, I've always said
two brothers and two sisters.

120
00:09:45,677 --> 00:09:47,159
Two brothers, two sisters.

121
00:09:49,021 --> 00:09:50,074
Here.

122
00:09:51,248 --> 00:09:52,423
What is this?

123
00:09:52,448 --> 00:09:54,714
- Your wedding gift money.
- What?

124
00:09:54,994 --> 00:09:56,940
Where would you get money for that?

125
00:09:57,280 --> 00:10:00,388
Sorry, it isn't much. Congratulations.

126
00:10:01,295 --> 00:10:02,368
Hey.

127
00:10:04,387 --> 00:10:05,719
Five hundred dollars?

128
00:10:06,275 --> 00:10:08,469
Who gives five hundred as a wedding gift?

129
00:10:08,494 --> 00:10:10,281
You're a student. Where's the money from?

130
00:10:12,564 --> 00:10:13,590
Here.

131
00:10:14,648 --> 00:10:17,439
What, am I supposed to buy gum with it?

132
00:10:18,008 --> 00:10:21,107
What do these two take me for?

133
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:27,399
- Hey!
- I don't want your lunch money.

134
00:10:27,505 --> 00:10:28,859
Pick it up. Now.

135
00:10:29,428 --> 00:10:31,754
Do you know
how hard Han Gyu Seo worked for that?

136
00:10:31,779 --> 00:10:35,863
That's why I don't want it. Move.

137
00:10:35,888 --> 00:10:37,155
Move, Han Gyu Min.

138
00:10:37,721 --> 00:10:41,053
You little beggars.

139
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:44,454
What? Beggars?

140
00:10:51,655 --> 00:10:53,545
Hey! Are you a dog?

141
00:10:53,834 --> 00:10:55,612
Why would you bite a person?

142
00:10:56,753 --> 00:10:59,432
- Kick me if you want to kick.
- Hey!

143
00:10:59,525 --> 00:11:02,765
Just try laying a hand on Gyu Seo.

144
00:11:03,107 --> 00:11:06,028
Hit me if you want to hit.
Until you feel better.

145
00:11:06,102 --> 00:11:08,696
What do you two think you're doing?

146
00:11:08,831 --> 00:11:13,260
I said let one of you cross me today,
and here you are.

147
00:11:13,285 --> 00:11:16,240
Why are you hitting the kids again?

148
00:11:17,015 --> 00:11:19,709
Hit me instead.

149
00:11:19,734 --> 00:11:22,657
I'm the root of all of it, so hit me.

150
00:11:22,682 --> 00:11:25,501
What is this childish nonsense?

151
00:11:25,622 --> 00:11:28,716
What, three against one?
You want to fight?

152
00:11:28,837 --> 00:11:31,930
What did the twins ever do?
Why go after the kids!

153
00:11:31,955 --> 00:11:34,088
Are the kids here for you to mess with?

154
00:11:34,113 --> 00:11:37,199
These two keep teaming up on me
and getting on my nerves!

155
00:11:37,288 --> 00:11:39,598
They're my kids, not yours!

156
00:11:39,623 --> 00:11:42,098
Who are you to keep going after my kids!

157
00:11:46,149 --> 00:11:49,335
I feel sick. I'm going to throw up.

158
00:11:49,362 --> 00:11:50,464
What.

159
00:11:50,881 --> 00:11:54,114
My stomach's already turning
from that Chinese food.

160
00:11:54,349 --> 00:11:56,555
Normally, I can hold my liquor.

161
00:11:56,580 --> 00:11:58,525
But now my stomach's all messed up!

162
00:11:58,939 --> 00:12:00,937
Hey.

163
00:12:00,962 --> 00:12:02,607
Hey.

164
00:12:02,632 --> 00:12:05,299
Don't we have a bowl? Bring one.

165
00:12:05,324 --> 00:12:08,104
Hold still. Hold it in.
Just a little longer.

166
00:12:08,129 --> 00:12:11,283
Hurry up and bring it.
Hold on a little. Don't move.

167
00:12:11,308 --> 00:12:13,471
Hey, a bowl.

168
00:13:29,022 --> 00:13:30,922
Gyeol doesn't look like he's waking up.

169
00:13:32,621 --> 00:13:37,134
You clipped his fingernails
and toenails so neatly.

170
00:13:38,341 --> 00:13:40,984
I was terrified I'd hurt him.

171
00:13:41,501 --> 00:13:43,546
How do you do something
that scary every time?

172
00:13:44,292 --> 00:13:45,861
Every mother does.

173
00:13:46,581 --> 00:13:48,534
I was shaking the first time too.

174
00:13:51,681 --> 00:13:52,982
Want some tea?

175
00:13:53,081 --> 00:13:54,791
I've got a really good chamomile.

176
00:14:13,447 --> 00:14:14,548
Sounds good.

177
00:14:19,407 --> 00:14:21,659
Do your shoelaces still come undone
like that?

178
00:14:22,191 --> 00:14:23,594
There they go again.

179
00:14:26,435 --> 00:14:29,214
I've never met anyone as busy as you.

180
00:14:29,641 --> 00:14:31,971
Too busy to even tie your shoes.

181
00:14:36,662 --> 00:14:40,242
From now on, I'll keep tying them for you.

182
00:14:43,288 --> 00:14:45,238
I can't stand worrying that you'll fall.

183
00:14:49,588 --> 00:14:51,554
I think I need to be beside you.

184
00:14:53,902 --> 00:14:59,054
Even if it costs me my life,

185
00:15:01,462 --> 00:15:03,145
I need to be there for you and Gyeol.

186
00:15:37,395 --> 00:15:40,263
What? Where did you
take a beating like this?

187
00:15:42,623 --> 00:15:45,592
Look at your face. Did that woman hit you?

188
00:15:45,637 --> 00:15:47,325
Hey, keep it down.

189
00:15:47,587 --> 00:15:48,789
Who was it?

190
00:15:48,951 --> 00:15:51,585
Who turned you into an ugly panda?

191
00:15:52,507 --> 00:15:54,265
You want the whole family to know?

192
00:15:54,582 --> 00:15:56,180
I said keep it down, punk.

193
00:16:03,869 --> 00:16:05,864
They got you good, everywhere.

194
00:16:10,395 --> 00:16:11,654
It's fine.

195
00:16:11,807 --> 00:16:13,674
You'll learn once you start working,

196
00:16:13,948 --> 00:16:16,402
sometimes you dish it out,
sometimes you take it.

197
00:16:16,488 --> 00:16:19,664
Are you a gangster now?
What, did you join the mob?

198
00:16:20,194 --> 00:16:21,671
I said keep it down.

199
00:16:21,957 --> 00:16:23,970
If Gyu Rim finds out, I'm in trouble.

200
00:16:23,995 --> 00:16:26,939
Gyu Rim isn't here.
She went on a trip with Gyeol.

201
00:16:27,188 --> 00:16:30,430
She's gone? Thank goodness.

202
00:16:30,908 --> 00:16:32,014
I thought I should've stayed out
for the night,

203
00:16:32,045 --> 00:16:33,467
wondering if I should've come home at all.

204
00:16:33,935 --> 00:16:35,817
Why sleep somewhere else
when you have a home?

205
00:16:36,328 --> 00:16:38,128
What have you done
to deserve sleeping elsewhere?

206
00:16:38,535 --> 00:16:39,834
You're really laying into me today.

207
00:16:45,615 --> 00:16:50,775
I wiped up Gyu Yeong's vomit once
this morning. Now it's your turn.

208
00:16:50,995 --> 00:16:53,049
I don't know what she mixed...

209
00:16:53,209 --> 00:16:55,922
- The smell...
- Fine.

210
00:17:01,715 --> 00:17:05,326
- Han Gyu Yeong threw up?
- Yes.

211
00:17:05,605 --> 00:17:07,055
She can really hold her liquor.

212
00:17:07,754 --> 00:17:11,104
Her stomach's lined with steel.
She almost never throws up.

213
00:17:15,862 --> 00:17:19,778
Fine. This is my best.
What are you going to do?

214
00:17:19,921 --> 00:17:22,898
Are you going to kill me or let me live?

215
00:17:27,682 --> 00:17:31,278
Nothing works on you.

216
00:17:31,347 --> 00:17:34,805
Just live
with the face you were born with.

217
00:17:39,661 --> 00:17:42,138
Hey.

218
00:17:42,841 --> 00:17:44,687
You're hopeless.

219
00:17:44,795 --> 00:17:46,960
Absolutely hopeless.

220
00:17:46,985 --> 00:17:48,236
Han Gyu Yeong!

221
00:17:52,574 --> 00:17:54,582
You scared me, you punk.

222
00:17:54,613 --> 00:17:56,579
I thought a patient who filed a complaint
came to kill me.

223
00:17:57,858 --> 00:18:00,715
What happened to your eye?

224
00:18:01,674 --> 00:18:02,723
Let's get hangover soup.

225
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:05,204
I'm not going.
First you hurt me, then you play doctor?

226
00:18:10,910 --> 00:18:11,988
Hey!

227
00:18:14,538 --> 00:18:16,184
That hits the spot.

228
00:18:16,209 --> 00:18:18,576
Cold noodles really are the best
for a hangover.

229
00:18:19,902 --> 00:18:23,448
So? You drank all that hard liquor alone?

230
00:18:24,008 --> 00:18:25,848
What else could I do when nobody came?

231
00:18:28,388 --> 00:18:33,049
Hey, do you know what Dad and the twins
ganged up and said to me last night?

232
00:18:33,875 --> 00:18:35,602
"They're my kids, not yours!"

233
00:18:35,642 --> 00:18:37,843
"Who are you to touch my kids!"

234
00:18:38,271 --> 00:18:40,558
So I'm not even his kid?

235
00:18:40,583 --> 00:18:42,198
It galls me. It's humiliating.

236
00:18:42,835 --> 00:18:46,615
Fine, let the three of them team up.
Han Gyu Rim, you and me on this side.

237
00:18:46,801 --> 00:18:48,862
No, Han Gyu Rim is on their side,

238
00:18:48,887 --> 00:18:50,829
so it's just you and me. Fine by me.

239
00:18:52,255 --> 00:18:55,769
Dad's actually making sense for once.
What's gotten into him?

240
00:18:56,062 --> 00:18:59,454
So why go after Dad's kids? Who are you?

241
00:19:00,206 --> 00:19:01,214
What, you punk?

242
00:19:01,393 --> 00:19:03,191
Instead of insulting the family,

243
00:19:03,302 --> 00:19:05,613
have you ever stopped
to ask what's wrong with you?

244
00:19:06,155 --> 00:19:08,335
You told people Father was dead
when he's very much alive,

245
00:19:08,587 --> 00:19:11,590
you cut off Gyu Rim and me
because we're beneath you,

246
00:19:11,641 --> 00:19:15,177
and you treat Gyu Seo and Gyu Min
like they're not even human. Who'd go?

247
00:19:15,902 --> 00:19:19,134
We come when you call and leave
when you say so? What are we, your dogs?

248
00:19:21,648 --> 00:19:24,108
People are staring.
Shut it and eat your noodles.

249
00:19:24,168 --> 00:19:26,285
How do I eat noodles with my mouth shut?

250
00:19:28,995 --> 00:19:32,702
Eat up, then get out. The sooner
you leave our house, the better.

251
00:19:41,048 --> 00:19:42,704
Seriously, Han Gyu O? Even you?

252
00:19:45,235 --> 00:19:49,636
Fine. Once I leave, I won't even spit
in the direction of this dump.

253
00:19:53,302 --> 00:19:54,920
One bottle of soju over here...

254
00:19:55,687 --> 00:19:58,047
No, I have work.

255
00:19:58,142 --> 00:20:01,599
More noodle broth over here.
Loaded with ice, make it freezing.

256
00:20:16,155 --> 00:20:20,339
Skip the ramen and have kimchi stew
with us. And rice.

257
00:20:20,868 --> 00:20:24,276
No, I'm fine. I've got no appetite,
so I'll just have ramen.

258
00:20:24,301 --> 00:20:27,018
I'll put tuna in the kimchi stew.

259
00:20:27,043 --> 00:20:30,275
Two cans, the kind with big chunks.

260
00:20:30,362 --> 00:20:31,696
Two whole cans of tuna?

261
00:20:31,721 --> 00:20:35,426
Yes. And tuna fritters too, coated in egg.

262
00:20:36,822 --> 00:20:40,993
Hey, make me an offer like that
and I'll cave right away.

263
00:20:42,308 --> 00:20:45,580
Tuna makes a really good salad too.

264
00:20:45,935 --> 00:20:47,829
Tuna rice roll is amazing.

265
00:20:47,854 --> 00:20:50,873
Tuna tastes good in absolutely anything.

266
00:20:52,975 --> 00:20:54,342
- Dad.
- Yes?

267
00:20:56,222 --> 00:20:59,439
Thanks for taking our side
against Han Gyu Yeong.

268
00:21:00,788 --> 00:21:02,173
That?

269
00:21:03,194 --> 00:21:04,819
That's just how it should be.

270
00:21:04,940 --> 00:21:07,531
Hey, you're my kid, not somebody else's.

271
00:21:08,222 --> 00:21:10,718
My fatherly love is no joke.

272
00:21:11,706 --> 00:21:13,922
Go on in. I'll call you when it's ready.

273
00:21:13,947 --> 00:21:17,394
So Gyu Rim went on a trip with just Gyeol?

274
00:21:18,256 --> 00:21:21,030
She could have called me. I love trips.

275
00:21:22,802 --> 00:21:25,381
Go in.

276
00:21:25,406 --> 00:21:28,175
- I already opened the ramen.
- I'll seal it back up.

277
00:22:45,105 --> 00:22:46,445
Mu Jin.

278
00:22:47,218 --> 00:22:49,218
You're up? Hungry?

279
00:22:52,772 --> 00:22:54,372
Where are we?

280
00:22:54,905 --> 00:22:57,372
Here? My house.

281
00:22:57,772 --> 00:23:00,764
The house I got ready
so I could bring you here.

282
00:23:05,060 --> 00:23:06,385
Is your mom still asleep?

283
00:23:06,672 --> 00:23:09,930
Yes. She must have been exhausted.

284
00:23:10,051 --> 00:23:15,151
Right. Your mom hasn't slept easy
since you came to my place.

285
00:23:16,272 --> 00:23:19,743
- Let's not wake her until she's ready.
- Okay.

286
00:23:21,872 --> 00:23:24,772
Sorry for bringing you here
without asking you.

287
00:23:24,872 --> 00:23:27,627
I love it. So much.

288
00:23:28,811 --> 00:23:31,162
Your mom said she'd call your teacher.

289
00:23:31,472 --> 00:23:32,472
Okay.

290
00:23:34,678 --> 00:23:38,857
But what about you?

291
00:23:39,104 --> 00:23:40,171
Why?

292
00:23:40,805 --> 00:23:43,037
Wouldn't Jeong Woo kick you out...

293
00:23:43,265 --> 00:23:46,358
if you keep skipping out like this?

294
00:23:47,772 --> 00:23:49,972
You're right. What do I do?

295
00:23:51,158 --> 00:23:54,051
I guess I'll have to beg. Beg real hard.

296
00:23:55,945 --> 00:23:57,612
- By the way.
- Yes.

297
00:23:58,772 --> 00:24:00,864
Do you smell something burning?

298
00:24:36,272 --> 00:24:38,474
Have I been asleep all this time?

299
00:24:42,372 --> 00:24:45,604
Gyeol. Han Gyeol.

300
00:25:07,772 --> 00:25:10,502
I was going to text,
but I thought I'd wake you.

301
00:25:10,672 --> 00:25:14,638
There's rice in the cooker,
and heat the soybean stew.

302
00:25:14,805 --> 00:25:17,762
Gyeol ate plenty, so don't worry.

303
00:25:22,104 --> 00:25:26,017
I read a novel a long time ago.
I don't even remember the title.

304
00:25:26,872 --> 00:25:29,927
The male lead says something like that
to the female lead.

305
00:25:31,705 --> 00:25:36,002
He says he'd give her half the time
he had left, just so she could sleep.

306
00:25:37,872 --> 00:25:42,156
The female lead was so busy with work
that she never got enough sleep.

307
00:25:52,154 --> 00:25:53,545
There are so many here.

308
00:25:57,305 --> 00:25:59,452
- There really are.
- Look.

309
00:26:00,263 --> 00:26:01,419
Amazing.

310
00:26:04,472 --> 00:26:07,072
There are a ton. Put them in.

311
00:26:07,986 --> 00:26:09,586
High five!

312
00:26:10,545 --> 00:26:14,935
That's how I felt, too.
I wanted you to get some sleep.

313
00:26:16,272 --> 00:26:21,940
You were always so exhausted,
I just wanted you to sleep soundly.

314
00:26:23,872 --> 00:26:25,405
Mom.

315
00:26:31,925 --> 00:26:34,825
Even if it meant giving you
all the time I had left.

316
00:26:56,972 --> 00:26:59,303
What did I do in a past life
to deserve this?

317
00:27:00,172 --> 00:27:04,005
What did I do to get stuck
with someone like Kim Mu Jin...

318
00:27:05,872 --> 00:27:09,872
As if being business partners
wasn't enough, now we're roommates...

319
00:27:12,772 --> 00:27:15,672
This awkwardness, this guilt...

320
00:27:16,072 --> 00:27:20,164
Why do I have to deal with
all this discomfort?

321
00:27:21,218 --> 00:27:24,353
I asked where Mu Jin went.
Why do you keep dodging?

322
00:27:25,472 --> 00:27:26,980
I told you I don't know.

323
00:27:27,005 --> 00:27:28,272
Why is his phone off?

324
00:27:28,372 --> 00:27:30,167
Did I turn it off?

325
00:27:30,472 --> 00:27:33,072
The battery died, or it broke, I guess.

326
00:27:50,605 --> 00:27:52,451
You said you were letting Mu Jin go.

327
00:27:52,972 --> 00:27:57,628
If you're letting him go, just let him go.
Don't be pathetic about it, please.

328
00:28:00,072 --> 00:28:03,557
Kim Mu Jin isn't my father's son.

329
00:28:04,512 --> 00:28:08,889
Dad lied. To protect my mother, his wife.

330
00:28:12,251 --> 00:28:13,693
So you know too.

331
00:28:15,077 --> 00:28:20,048
Gyu Rim being your mother's real daughter
makes far more sense.

332
00:28:20,505 --> 00:28:22,292
You knew too?

333
00:28:24,872 --> 00:28:26,534
What did I just say?

334
00:28:26,972 --> 00:28:28,461
Does Mu Jin know too?

335
00:28:30,345 --> 00:28:33,777
My stomach hurts.
I need to go to the bathroom.

336
00:28:35,672 --> 00:28:39,720
Mu Jin and you both knew and made
a fool of me this whole time?

337
00:28:39,745 --> 00:28:42,245
Seo Hyeon, I found out yesterday.

338
00:28:43,532 --> 00:28:45,884
Just accept it and let go, please.

339
00:28:46,458 --> 00:28:49,837
Either way, you and Mu Jin can't happen.

340
00:29:09,818 --> 00:29:11,278
Code red.

341
00:29:11,303 --> 00:29:14,147
Seo Hyeon knows everything
about her mother and Gyu Rim.

342
00:29:14,172 --> 00:29:17,238
She's completely lost it. No fixing this.

343
00:29:17,272 --> 00:29:20,747
Don't come to Seoul. Stay put
and keep a low profile for a while.

344
00:29:20,772 --> 00:29:22,972
No, just move abroad.

345
00:29:23,405 --> 00:29:26,024
No, just leave the planet.

346
00:29:29,772 --> 00:29:31,405
(Power Off)

347
00:29:36,472 --> 00:29:37,604
Is it that good?

348
00:29:37,705 --> 00:29:43,147
Yes, it's so good. So much fun.
I'm so happy.

349
00:29:46,145 --> 00:29:49,408
But I'm so tired.

350
00:29:49,525 --> 00:29:52,837
Can I sleep until the dough soup is ready?

351
00:29:53,183 --> 00:29:55,123
Of course you can.

352
00:30:08,505 --> 00:30:10,694
- Where's Gyeol?
- He must be worn out.

353
00:30:10,872 --> 00:30:13,072
He's sleeping until the soup is ready.

354
00:30:14,372 --> 00:30:16,247
Let me do it. You rest, too.

355
00:30:16,272 --> 00:30:20,057
Forget it. I said don't lift a finger.

356
00:30:20,250 --> 00:30:21,690
Don't do anything.

357
00:30:23,845 --> 00:30:26,078
Want some coffee?
Should I make you coffee?

358
00:30:28,018 --> 00:30:31,882
Let me move a little.
I'll seize up at this rate.

359
00:30:33,472 --> 00:30:35,072
Then I'll make the coffee.

360
00:30:39,671 --> 00:30:41,157
Do me one favor, Gyu Rim.

361
00:30:55,191 --> 00:30:59,207
A lot of things will come your way
and shake you.

362
00:31:01,398 --> 00:31:02,875
But don't let them shake you.

363
00:31:12,318 --> 00:31:15,942
Don't look at anything.
Don't listen to anything.

364
00:31:18,317 --> 00:31:20,978
Just look at me, listen only to me.

365
00:31:23,472 --> 00:31:24,827
You can do that for me, right?

366
00:31:59,172 --> 00:32:00,438
What are you doing?

367
00:32:02,505 --> 00:32:03,972
Why are you packing?

368
00:32:05,671 --> 00:32:06,671
Honey.

369
00:32:11,772 --> 00:32:14,329
Are you really leaving
because Seo Hyeon said to?

370
00:32:14,472 --> 00:32:16,284
Were you always this irresponsible?

371
00:32:18,289 --> 00:32:19,745
If I just disappear,

372
00:32:21,172 --> 00:32:23,353
everything will be okay.

373
00:32:23,472 --> 00:32:25,572
What exactly gets solved if you disappear?

374
00:32:26,872 --> 00:32:28,015
Honey.

375
00:32:29,082 --> 00:32:31,915
When you decided
to tell Seo Hyeon the truth,

376
00:32:32,072 --> 00:32:34,554
did you not think she'd fall apart
like this?

377
00:32:34,805 --> 00:32:37,664
She's already half out of her mind.
Anything could come out of her mouth.

378
00:32:37,772 --> 00:32:40,472
Did you not prepare yourself for that?

379
00:32:42,405 --> 00:32:46,254
I thought about it. I prepared myself.

380
00:32:46,758 --> 00:32:50,987
Whatever Seo Hyeon threw at me,
I'd swallow it, take it, hold on.

381
00:32:52,072 --> 00:32:56,205
I tried so hard to be shameless
and just let it go...

382
00:32:58,272 --> 00:32:59,742
I can't do it.

383
00:33:00,228 --> 00:33:03,135
I can't watch Seo Hyeon suffer
because of me.

384
00:33:04,385 --> 00:33:07,890
I can't bear to see her get hurt,

385
00:33:08,764 --> 00:33:11,510
and suffer because of me.

386
00:33:11,535 --> 00:33:13,111
None of it is because of you.

387
00:33:13,956 --> 00:33:15,704
What did you actually do?

388
00:33:16,372 --> 00:33:18,034
How did you raise Seo Hyeon?

389
00:33:18,825 --> 00:33:21,471
As if she'd break if you held her,
or fly away if you breathed on her.

390
00:33:21,985 --> 00:33:25,125
You raised her with such care,
always worrying about her.

391
00:33:25,891 --> 00:33:28,859
And you even cut ties
with your own children,

392
00:33:29,672 --> 00:33:32,005
and lived that way, all for Seo Hyeon.

393
00:33:32,705 --> 00:33:34,144
I know that.

394
00:33:38,531 --> 00:33:42,031
They say you're going
to be my mom from now on?

395
00:33:42,572 --> 00:33:46,201
That's right, Seo Hyeon. Let's get along.

396
00:33:49,772 --> 00:33:52,572
They say you have a daughter my age.

397
00:33:54,472 --> 00:34:00,303
Yes, I do. She's exactly your age.

398
00:34:06,572 --> 00:34:08,690
What's wrong?

399
00:34:08,715 --> 00:34:11,803
Did I do something wrong?

400
00:34:12,172 --> 00:34:14,914
Is it that you don't like me?

401
00:34:15,805 --> 00:34:21,472
If you don't want me to,
I won't marry your father.

402
00:34:21,772 --> 00:34:24,139
I'll never do anything you don't want.

403
00:34:26,172 --> 00:34:30,641
It's not that.
I have a friend named Choi In Ju.

404
00:34:31,572 --> 00:34:34,955
Her parents divorced too
and she got a stepmother,

405
00:34:35,705 --> 00:34:40,352
and the stepmother treats In Ju
and her own child completely differently.

406
00:34:41,372 --> 00:34:46,674
All the good food and pretty things
go to her own child.

407
00:34:47,732 --> 00:34:51,832
In Ju was so upset she told her dad,
and her dad said this.

408
00:34:52,172 --> 00:34:55,825
"Loving the child you bore more
is just human nature."

409
00:34:56,985 --> 00:34:59,452
"That's only natural.
You should understand."

410
00:35:09,172 --> 00:35:10,272
Don't cry.

411
00:35:10,297 --> 00:35:13,477
(Jang Seo Hyeon)

412
00:35:18,965 --> 00:35:23,185
I can accept being treated differently.
It's human nature.

413
00:35:24,672 --> 00:35:26,867
At least I get to have a mom.

414
00:35:28,005 --> 00:35:33,705
My mother was sick when I was five,
so I missed having a mother so much.

415
00:35:42,972 --> 00:35:48,510
Honey, there's no villain here.

416
00:35:49,872 --> 00:35:55,372
Gyu Rim, you, Seo Hyeon, Mu Jin, me,
none of it is anyone's fault.

417
00:35:56,105 --> 00:36:02,603
Our lives got tangled in a way
that's hard to believe, and it's a mess,

418
00:36:03,272 --> 00:36:05,072
but we've all worked hard at living.

419
00:36:05,872 --> 00:36:10,005
All you're guilty of is raising Seo Hyeon
with everything you had.

420
00:36:12,205 --> 00:36:13,272
Honey.

421
00:36:15,272 --> 00:36:18,272
If there's anyone you should apologize to,

422
00:36:20,472 --> 00:36:22,505
it's the children you gave birth to,

423
00:36:23,472 --> 00:36:26,657
especially Gyu Rim.

424
00:36:27,331 --> 00:36:29,104
Gyu Rim is the only one.

425
00:37:25,872 --> 00:37:28,247
You think I had you just to peel garlic?

426
00:37:28,272 --> 00:37:29,463
What's with you?

427
00:37:29,810 --> 00:37:32,730
Did Gyu Rim's mother have her
just to peel garlic, too?

428
00:37:35,272 --> 00:37:38,678
Then you think
I went through childbirth...

429
00:37:38,719 --> 00:37:41,552
just so you could shield Han Gyu Rim?

430
00:37:42,512 --> 00:37:43,844
Then did Gyu Rim's mother have her...

431
00:37:44,072 --> 00:37:49,362
just to be bullied
by an old witch like you?

432
00:37:49,505 --> 00:37:50,902
A witch?

433
00:37:51,089 --> 00:37:54,580
Did this rotten boy just call me a witch?

434
00:37:54,605 --> 00:37:59,472
Gyu Rim trusts you and looks up to you
like her own mother,

435
00:37:59,672 --> 00:38:02,872
and you do nothing but push her around.

436
00:38:02,905 --> 00:38:04,905
How am I supposed to go easy on her?

437
00:38:05,025 --> 00:38:08,374
We're so busy today,
and she just skips work.

438
00:38:08,572 --> 00:38:11,272
Busy? There isn't a single customer.

439
00:38:12,205 --> 00:38:18,172
She called last night to say
she couldn't make it to work today.

440
00:38:18,305 --> 00:38:21,305
She told us beforehand.
How is that skipping work?

441
00:38:21,572 --> 00:38:25,505
Why don't you quit fooling around
and take the bar exam?

442
00:38:25,772 --> 00:38:27,886
Watching you defend Han Gyu Rim,

443
00:38:27,931 --> 00:38:31,580
you'd be a huge success as a lawyer.

444
00:38:31,605 --> 00:38:35,272
No. I'll just help you out
and take it easy.

445
00:38:35,505 --> 00:38:39,626
If I do too well, you'll get a big head
and that won't do.

446
00:38:43,005 --> 00:38:47,061
They say your worst enemies
come back as your children.

447
00:38:48,091 --> 00:38:50,691
My rotten luck.

448
00:38:51,072 --> 00:38:53,252
Honestly, Mother...

449
00:38:55,672 --> 00:38:57,472
My rotten luck.

450
00:39:01,472 --> 00:39:04,172
Ma'am.

451
00:39:05,372 --> 00:39:09,998
A golden pig turned
into a dragon and flew up?

452
00:39:12,678 --> 00:39:14,008
This is yours, ma'am.

453
00:39:16,518 --> 00:39:22,285
He looks like some scruffy little rat.
Hardly looks like a future big shot.

454
00:39:35,505 --> 00:39:37,283
Let's put it in writing.

455
00:39:37,314 --> 00:39:39,416
That you won't torment Gyu Rim,
and that her family...

456
00:39:41,372 --> 00:39:42,978
What's wrong with you?
Did you have a stroke?

457
00:39:43,272 --> 00:39:44,972
Pinch me.

458
00:39:46,872 --> 00:39:48,631
You pinch me, Mom.

459
00:39:48,672 --> 00:39:50,372
- Right?
- Right.

460
00:39:52,472 --> 00:39:56,394
- A thousand dollars!
- A thousand dollars!

461
00:39:56,972 --> 00:39:58,372
Mother.

462
00:39:58,772 --> 00:40:01,005
Is this a dream, or is this real?

463
00:40:01,030 --> 00:40:03,780
How on earth did I win the lottery?

464
00:40:03,805 --> 00:40:07,672
Mom, I've never actually met
someone who won the lottery.

465
00:40:07,705 --> 00:40:09,372
- That dream was right.
- What dream?

466
00:40:09,447 --> 00:40:13,047
He dreamed a pig turned into a dragon
and flew up to the sky.

467
00:40:13,072 --> 00:40:15,072
Unbelievable.

468
00:40:15,105 --> 00:40:17,372
Who had the dragon dream?

469
00:40:17,431 --> 00:40:23,331
Gyeol's grandfather did.
He bought two tickets and gave me one.

470
00:40:23,572 --> 00:40:26,723
Gyeol's grandfather? Gyu Rim's father?

471
00:40:29,405 --> 00:40:32,847
I think I shouldn't have said anything.

472
00:40:32,872 --> 00:40:35,272
Then you have to split it with him.

473
00:40:35,472 --> 00:40:38,472
Hold on, I will call him and tell him
the ticket he gave you won, quickly...

474
00:40:38,505 --> 00:40:40,307
He didn't ask for half.

475
00:40:40,332 --> 00:40:44,362
He just asked to stay in his current home
if the ticket won.

476
00:40:44,972 --> 00:40:49,007
Really? Amazing.
Gyu Rim's father really came through.

477
00:40:49,372 --> 00:40:51,026
Don't say a word for now.

478
00:40:51,172 --> 00:40:54,347
I'll handle it, so you keep quiet.

479
00:40:54,372 --> 00:40:56,805
Just shut your mouth
and go home and relax.

480
00:40:56,838 --> 00:40:57,847
(Song Il Gook)

481
00:40:57,872 --> 00:40:59,572
- Watch a TV drama or something.
- Sure.

482
00:40:59,612 --> 00:41:01,805
- Or borrow some comic books.
- Understood.

483
00:41:01,830 --> 00:41:04,489
I'll wash up and read comics
until I sleep.

484
00:41:17,645 --> 00:41:21,733
Why have you two been staring
at me like this?

485
00:41:21,998 --> 00:41:23,846
Ever since you walked in,

486
00:41:23,993 --> 00:41:27,707
have you noticed
you've been staring at me?

487
00:41:28,705 --> 00:41:31,843
- Is there something on my face?
- No.

488
00:41:32,472 --> 00:41:34,272
I'm sorry.

489
00:41:34,972 --> 00:41:38,772
You look so much like someone I know.

490
00:41:39,572 --> 00:41:44,072
You look so familiar to me, too.
I'm sorry.

491
00:41:44,705 --> 00:41:46,954
I don't have a very common face.

492
00:41:47,114 --> 00:41:49,101
Who could I look so much like?

493
00:41:49,572 --> 00:41:51,906
I do get told I look like Angelina Jolie.

494
00:41:53,811 --> 00:41:55,182
Jolie?

495
00:41:59,472 --> 00:42:03,572
I lived in Pohang for a while as a kid,

496
00:42:04,205 --> 00:42:08,005
and you look exactly like
the Korean teacher who boarded with us.

497
00:42:08,371 --> 00:42:11,938
Ms. Seo Hye Suk. I had a crush on her.

498
00:42:12,205 --> 00:42:14,380
Have you ever lived in Pohang?

499
00:42:16,872 --> 00:42:19,705
And you? Who do I look like to you?

500
00:42:20,078 --> 00:42:22,948
Well, you look just like the mother of...

501
00:42:23,005 --> 00:42:28,372
my friend Shin Jun Yeong,
who ran a spicy beef soup place.

502
00:42:31,120 --> 00:42:32,247
Are they twins?

503
00:42:32,272 --> 00:42:36,505
I'll take it as a compliment that you both
feel that comfortable with me.

504
00:42:36,505 --> 00:42:37,605
Sure.

505
00:42:41,272 --> 00:42:45,549
Joel, I'm a bit ambitious.

506
00:42:45,972 --> 00:42:50,105
There's one rival brand that bothers me
enough to keep me up at night.

507
00:42:50,272 --> 00:42:53,937
I want to crush it completely
through this collaboration.

508
00:42:54,464 --> 00:42:56,171
Do you think you can do that?

509
00:42:59,605 --> 00:43:00,672
I'll have to try and see.

510
00:43:00,672 --> 00:43:03,572
Yes, he can. Don't worry. Get some sleep.

511
00:43:04,372 --> 00:43:06,572
How do you know if I can
without even trying?

512
00:43:06,572 --> 00:43:08,672
He just tells you
that anything is possible.

513
00:43:08,672 --> 00:43:10,785
- Are you a con man?
- Joel.

514
00:43:12,972 --> 00:43:14,441
I'll have to try and see.

515
00:43:19,172 --> 00:43:22,272
I love how honest you are.

516
00:43:22,972 --> 00:43:26,972
I like this man a lot myself.

517
00:43:29,172 --> 00:43:32,572
You said you aren't married yet, right?

518
00:43:33,072 --> 00:43:36,641
- Are you seeing anyone?
- No, I'm not.

519
00:43:37,205 --> 00:43:41,121
This is my daughter.
Would you like to meet her?

520
00:43:41,672 --> 00:43:42,872
Chairwoman Hong.

521
00:43:46,972 --> 00:43:50,080
I appreciate the offer, but no, thank you.

522
00:43:50,340 --> 00:43:51,867
We should keep business
and personal matters separate.

523
00:43:57,078 --> 00:44:00,091
Poor you. You got rejected
before you could even confess.

524
00:44:08,825 --> 00:44:11,223
Wash up over here, Mother.

525
00:44:17,594 --> 00:44:19,172
Any luck?

526
00:44:22,305 --> 00:44:25,279
- I've got a belly, don't I?
- Not at all.

527
00:44:25,805 --> 00:44:27,347
Mother, would you like to try this?

528
00:44:27,372 --> 00:44:30,372
A college classmate of mine made it
and gave me a few bottles.

529
00:44:30,572 --> 00:44:34,772
It's all organic, plant-based,
and they say it works wonders.

530
00:44:35,584 --> 00:44:40,428
If they're your college classmate,
they must be a doctor too, right?

531
00:44:40,472 --> 00:44:41,472
Yes, of course.

532
00:44:41,998 --> 00:44:44,183
Thank you, sweetheart.

533
00:44:45,272 --> 00:44:46,905
Did you change your perfume?

534
00:44:47,119 --> 00:44:49,334
- It smells good, doesn't it? One moment.
- Yes.

535
00:44:49,425 --> 00:44:51,789
Turn around, Mother.

536
00:44:53,231 --> 00:44:55,221
So luxurious.

537
00:44:55,972 --> 00:44:59,631
It's Chanel's latest fragrance.
It's yours, Mother.

538
00:45:00,808 --> 00:45:03,401
It suits you better than me.

539
00:45:04,440 --> 00:45:07,407
How did I get such
a thoughtful daughter-in-law?

540
00:45:08,108 --> 00:45:12,695
Your father must be so busy
running a company,

541
00:45:12,856 --> 00:45:16,768
but he raised his children so well.

542
00:45:16,955 --> 00:45:20,597
You know I'd never hesitate
to give you anything, right?

543
00:45:20,622 --> 00:45:21,875
I'm touched.

544
00:45:21,961 --> 00:45:23,865
- Ready to go?
- Yes.

545
00:45:31,361 --> 00:45:35,518
That woman. "I'm touched." So dramatic.

546
00:45:36,770 --> 00:45:38,008
You think you're the only one
with a daughter-in-law?

547
00:45:38,042 --> 00:45:40,082
Nobody else has one, just you?

548
00:45:42,161 --> 00:45:45,228
What on earth is that Mu Jin doing?

549
00:45:51,168 --> 00:45:53,354
You were so late,
I thought something happened.

550
00:45:53,382 --> 00:45:57,435
Hey, is there any way to ruin Mu Jin?

551
00:45:57,567 --> 00:45:59,308
Ruin him so completely...

552
00:45:59,333 --> 00:46:03,354
that he comes crawling back to me
on his knees.

553
00:46:04,868 --> 00:46:07,644
Solids have tighter molecular bonds
than liquids.

554
00:46:07,669 --> 00:46:11,183
Normally, a stone thrown like this
beats the water's surface tension...

555
00:46:12,827 --> 00:46:14,613
and sinks right in. But...

556
00:46:14,638 --> 00:46:15,767
Hold on.

557
00:46:16,114 --> 00:46:18,909
You throw this flat stone
at the lowest angle,

558
00:46:18,934 --> 00:46:21,584
so the contact area between the water
and the stone gets wider,

559
00:46:21,609 --> 00:46:23,196
keeping theta as small as possible.

560
00:46:23,221 --> 00:46:24,534
So theta means...

561
00:46:25,001 --> 00:46:26,995
Is it sine theta? Cosine...

562
00:46:29,081 --> 00:46:31,396
- You didn't understand a word, did you?
- No.

563
00:46:31,534 --> 00:46:32,831
Sorry about that.

564
00:46:33,079 --> 00:46:36,621
First, find the flattest stone you can.

565
00:46:36,646 --> 00:46:39,879
That kind works best for skipping.

566
00:46:40,116 --> 00:46:41,476
Give it a throw.

567
00:46:44,208 --> 00:46:47,501
- One more. Try a heavier stone.
- Okay.

568
00:46:49,481 --> 00:46:50,717
Watch.

569
00:46:50,997 --> 00:46:54,960
Hook the edge with your fingers
and grip it like a baseball.

570
00:46:54,985 --> 00:47:00,661
Get low so the stone lines up
with the surface. A low angle.

571
00:47:00,686 --> 00:47:03,784
Throw from up high and your center wobbles
and the angle goes up.

572
00:47:04,141 --> 00:47:07,426
Get low and steady, then fast. Snap!

573
00:47:08,614 --> 00:47:10,101
- Want to try, Gyeol?
- Yes.

574
00:47:20,028 --> 00:47:22,695
Mom, did you see?

575
00:47:22,720 --> 00:47:25,365
Yes, I saw. You're the best, Gyeol.

576
00:47:26,228 --> 00:47:29,008
One more time. I need a stone.

577
00:47:30,446 --> 00:47:31,879
She laughed. Han Gyu Rim laughed.

578
00:47:32,974 --> 00:47:34,691
I finally made her laugh.

579
00:47:35,621 --> 00:47:36,994
Let's try one more.

580
00:47:40,775 --> 00:47:41,847
What is this?

581
00:47:43,302 --> 00:47:44,966
The money you bought Han Gyu O with.

582
00:47:50,629 --> 00:47:52,990
It isn't counterfeit,
so no need to doubt it.

583
00:47:53,519 --> 00:47:54,845
What is this, exactly?

584
00:47:56,108 --> 00:47:58,574
If you're asking
where the money came from,

585
00:47:58,609 --> 00:48:00,799
I took out a bank loan a little while ago.

586
00:48:01,686 --> 00:48:04,398
If you're asking why I'm giving it to you,

587
00:48:05,433 --> 00:48:08,546
it's to buy Han Gyu O back.

588
00:48:11,515 --> 00:48:13,409
Have you lost your mind?

589
00:48:13,981 --> 00:48:15,362
Han Gyu O isn't an object.

590
00:48:15,382 --> 00:48:17,268
You treat him like one,

591
00:48:17,421 --> 00:48:20,078
which is why you threw insane money
at him and bought him.

592
00:48:21,127 --> 00:48:24,334
- Okay.
- Let's settle it your way.

593
00:48:24,907 --> 00:48:27,500
Money for money.

594
00:48:29,814 --> 00:48:31,587
You said you didn't want Han Gyu O.

595
00:48:31,964 --> 00:48:35,481
You were avoiding him before.
So what are you doing now?

596
00:48:36,494 --> 00:48:38,394
You made me realize something.

597
00:48:39,835 --> 00:48:42,013
I don't want to give Han Gyu O to anyone.

598
00:48:43,237 --> 00:48:44,925
Least of all to Seo Min Ju.

599
00:48:45,780 --> 00:48:48,825
I don't want to, whatever it costs me.

600
00:48:54,128 --> 00:48:55,536
I won't sell.

601
00:48:56,361 --> 00:48:58,447
I'd never sell Han Gyu O to you.

602
00:49:00,128 --> 00:49:02,185
You took the money, so it's done.

603
00:49:05,621 --> 00:49:07,777
That girl. Hey!

604
00:49:08,251 --> 00:49:11,238
(Don't wake me
unless the house is on fire)

605
00:49:19,628 --> 00:49:22,382
Don't wake me unless the house is on fire.

606
00:49:28,321 --> 00:49:30,755
That ugly face got even uglier.

607
00:50:03,548 --> 00:50:04,780
What time is it?

608
00:50:05,522 --> 00:50:07,442
What does a jobless man need the time for?

609
00:50:07,779 --> 00:50:09,086
Go back to sleep.

610
00:50:10,374 --> 00:50:12,188
Sleep. Deeply.

611
00:50:13,261 --> 00:50:16,912
<i>Hush-a-bye, hush-a-bye, hush-a-bye</i>

612
00:50:33,008 --> 00:50:34,802
What's his password?

613
00:50:35,725 --> 00:50:39,637
He hates birthdays and anniversaries
way more than you'd expect.

614
00:50:40,098 --> 00:50:42,230
Something way simpler than you'd think.

615
00:50:44,113 --> 00:50:45,574
Five zeros?

616
00:50:46,182 --> 00:50:48,262
One to six? No.

617
00:50:51,348 --> 00:50:54,324
Five, six, seven, eight, nine, zero?
No way.

618
00:50:58,034 --> 00:50:59,497
Five, six, seven, eight, nine, zero?

619
00:51:00,556 --> 00:51:04,380
A man whose life is that complicated
has 567890 as a password?

620
00:51:25,816 --> 00:51:28,470
- What?
- Bugs will fly in. Close your mouth.

621
00:51:30,290 --> 00:51:34,439
So Gyu O is one of those men in movies,

622
00:51:34,464 --> 00:51:37,315
- who seduce women and drain them...
- That isn't the point right now.

623
00:51:37,340 --> 00:51:39,751
How is that not the point?

624
00:51:40,455 --> 00:51:41,899
My own brother...

625
00:51:42,337 --> 00:51:44,795
My brother is a host bar escort,
and that's not...

626
00:51:44,802 --> 00:51:46,375
Hey, say it louder.

627
00:51:46,635 --> 00:51:48,895
Let Gyu O and the whole family hear you.

628
00:51:48,975 --> 00:51:51,461
Make sure every neighbor knows.
Let everyone find out.

629
00:51:54,521 --> 00:51:57,866
I'm just as angry and upset as you,
and I'm going crazy too,

630
00:51:57,961 --> 00:52:00,333
and I want to kill Gyu O myself,

631
00:52:00,594 --> 00:52:04,481
I feel the same way you do,
but he had his reasons.

632
00:52:05,013 --> 00:52:06,277
What reasons?

633
00:52:06,681 --> 00:52:08,845
What reason could there be
for something that insane?

634
00:52:10,181 --> 00:52:13,317
Of all people, Gyu O...

635
00:52:13,542 --> 00:52:16,168
How could my own brother do this?

636
00:52:16,441 --> 00:52:18,088
If Gyu Rim finds out...

637
00:52:18,113 --> 00:52:20,796
- Hey, if Gyu Rim finds out?
- She'd die.

638
00:52:21,943 --> 00:52:23,754
Gyu Rim would drop dead.

639
00:52:26,021 --> 00:52:27,935
That's why I wanted to talk
it through with you.

640
00:52:27,948 --> 00:52:29,668
Because you're smarter than me.

641
00:53:20,812 --> 00:53:23,610
I took photos with my phone.
The messages on Gyu O's phone.

642
00:53:25,288 --> 00:53:28,173
Eight years ago, he got into a fight
with a man named Son Ji Yeol,

643
00:53:28,301 --> 00:53:29,740
while saving a friend.

644
00:53:29,821 --> 00:53:32,312
And the man got hit
and hurt his head badly.

645
00:53:46,401 --> 00:53:51,005
Since then, he's covered his surgery,
hospital bills, and treatment costs,

646
00:53:51,935 --> 00:53:54,157
and when he ran out of money,
he even borrowed from loan sharks.

647
00:53:55,178 --> 00:53:57,766
And to pay off those loans,
he had no choice...

648
00:54:05,515 --> 00:54:07,201
He dropped out of high school.

649
00:54:07,348 --> 00:54:10,114
How was he supposed to earn that kind
of money with no diploma?

650
00:54:12,182 --> 00:54:14,982
The one who hurt
a weaker person first was the bad guy.

651
00:54:15,181 --> 00:54:17,209
It happened while he was saving a friend,

652
00:54:17,234 --> 00:54:19,664
so he shouldn't have to carry all of it.

653
00:54:19,761 --> 00:54:21,777
The man he hit was an orphan.

654
00:54:22,468 --> 00:54:24,088
No parents, no siblings.

655
00:54:24,509 --> 00:54:29,022
Still, how is he being
this much of a sucker?

656
00:54:29,568 --> 00:54:31,668
From the messages, even recently,

657
00:54:31,709 --> 00:54:34,247
he was wiring huge amounts
to the man's wife.

658
00:54:34,458 --> 00:54:37,902
Maybe Gyu O is the one
who took a hit to the head.

659
00:54:39,175 --> 00:54:40,495
Where are you going?

660
00:54:40,554 --> 00:54:43,098
To tell Gyu O he's an idiot,

661
00:54:43,123 --> 00:54:45,008
and to snap out of it.

662
00:54:45,033 --> 00:54:47,870
If he knows you found out too,
he'll want to crawl into a hole.

663
00:54:47,895 --> 00:54:49,508
Then what am I supposed to do,

664
00:54:49,533 --> 00:54:51,582
what do you want from me?

665
00:54:52,496 --> 00:54:54,054
You shouldn't have told me, then.

666
00:54:54,219 --> 00:54:56,210
You should have kept me in the dark.

667
00:54:56,868 --> 00:55:01,322
This is killing me. It really is.

668
00:55:05,968 --> 00:55:08,126
You're still a minute older than me.

669
00:55:08,151 --> 00:55:10,344
I thought you'd know the answer.

670
00:55:11,555 --> 00:55:13,180
It was too hard carrying it alone,

671
00:55:13,459 --> 00:55:15,592
like I'd burst.

672
00:55:22,128 --> 00:55:25,341
Hey, I'm sorry.
I should have kept it to myself.

673
00:55:25,366 --> 00:55:27,856
- It hurts.
- It's my fault.

674
00:55:28,880 --> 00:55:31,642
What do we do about him?

675
00:55:48,962 --> 00:55:51,615
You've got thirteen
missed calls, haven't you?

676
00:55:51,739 --> 00:55:53,103
Why haven't you called back?

677
00:55:55,029 --> 00:55:56,263
Because I didn't want to.

678
00:55:56,975 --> 00:55:59,605
- Hey!
- Don't call me for a while.

679
00:56:00,595 --> 00:56:02,337
Did Kwon Hui Na call you?

680
00:56:03,934 --> 00:56:06,915
That lunatic bought you off me.

681
00:56:07,128 --> 00:56:08,804
Didn't she say anything?

682
00:56:21,281 --> 00:56:23,470
What is it? Pink eye?

683
00:56:24,101 --> 00:56:26,478
I cursed you to drop dead from illness,

684
00:56:26,539 --> 00:56:28,189
and all you got was pink eye?

685
00:56:28,734 --> 00:56:30,400
I hear you gave money to Seo Min Ju.

686
00:56:30,740 --> 00:56:32,150
You even took out a loan.

687
00:56:34,054 --> 00:56:35,911
She told you about the loan too?

688
00:56:36,317 --> 00:56:39,730
Fine, must be nice to have so much money.

689
00:56:39,908 --> 00:56:42,265
But that's her mother's money, not hers.

690
00:56:43,209 --> 00:56:45,893
- Why did you do it?
- None of your business.

691
00:56:46,868 --> 00:56:48,328
Do you like me?

692
00:56:48,675 --> 00:56:49,955
Are you on something?

693
00:56:50,361 --> 00:56:52,857
Am I insane, liking human garbage
like you?

694
00:56:54,954 --> 00:56:56,145
Exactly.

695
00:56:59,055 --> 00:57:00,341
Take the money back.

696
00:57:00,468 --> 00:57:02,504
I'm not even worth that much.

697
00:57:03,448 --> 00:57:04,987
That's what I came to say.

698
00:57:08,481 --> 00:57:10,908
Whether you're worth it is mine to decide.

699
00:57:15,461 --> 00:57:16,790
Do you have money to burn?

700
00:57:17,521 --> 00:57:20,969
How much do you make a month?
That's a lot of money for you.

701
00:57:21,554 --> 00:57:23,131
Take the money back. Right now.

702
00:57:23,622 --> 00:57:26,185
It's my money to spend.
What business is it of yours?

703
00:57:26,447 --> 00:57:27,639
You're an object.

704
00:57:30,875 --> 00:57:32,998
Bought and sold with money.
What else is that?

705
00:57:33,741 --> 00:57:36,641
You're an object, Han Gyu O.

706
00:57:37,808 --> 00:57:39,856
Something small and worthless
I can throw away anytime,

707
00:57:40,366 --> 00:57:43,283
the moment I get bored of you.

708
00:57:51,733 --> 00:57:53,184
I'll say this one last time.

709
00:57:54,166 --> 00:57:57,437
- Take the money back.
- No.

710
00:58:00,514 --> 00:58:02,327
I'll tell your parents.

711
00:58:02,441 --> 00:58:05,876
That their daughter is ruining her life
over human garbage,

712
00:58:05,984 --> 00:58:07,442
and they need to come stop you.

713
00:58:07,467 --> 00:58:08,716
Fine, tell them.

714
00:58:08,741 --> 00:58:10,839
How would you even know
where my parents are.

715
00:58:10,864 --> 00:58:14,057
Su Nam would give me a phone number
at least, if I asked.

716
00:58:14,082 --> 00:58:16,407
- Hey, that's low.
- I follow through.

717
00:58:16,967 --> 00:58:18,416
Get it back before the day is out.

718
00:58:20,975 --> 00:58:22,750
Then don't see Seo Min Ju.

719
00:58:24,061 --> 00:58:26,501
You're mine, and I'm going to like you.

720
00:58:31,567 --> 00:58:33,199
I'm going to be
the only one who likes you.

721
00:58:38,128 --> 00:58:39,725
Just try seeing Seo Min Ju.

722
00:58:39,961 --> 00:58:42,079
Then you die and I die.

723
00:59:06,108 --> 00:59:07,474
- Mu Jin.
- Yes.

724
00:59:07,575 --> 00:59:10,676
Let's run away again sometime.
Somewhere nobody knows us.

725
00:59:10,853 --> 00:59:13,655
- Gyeol.
- Sure. Let's do that.

726
00:59:43,162 --> 00:59:44,517
Go on in.

727
00:59:45,383 --> 00:59:46,983
Go on in. See you again.

728
00:59:47,008 --> 00:59:49,958
- Yes. Take care. Thank you.
- Sure.

729
00:59:51,661 --> 00:59:53,361
Gyeol, do you want to go in first?

730
00:59:53,428 --> 00:59:55,288
I'll talk with Mu Jin for a bit.

731
00:59:55,434 --> 00:59:56,796
Okay, got it.

732
01:00:02,373 --> 01:00:04,620
(Top prize, 500,000 Dollars)

733
01:00:11,202 --> 01:00:13,567
Seriously.

734
01:00:14,970 --> 01:00:17,952
The dragon was rising and took a detour.

735
01:00:18,554 --> 01:00:22,005
Not even a booby prize. What is this?

736
01:00:22,030 --> 01:00:25,401
If I ever buy a lottery ticket again,

737
01:00:25,501 --> 01:00:27,336
I'll be Gyeol's grandson.

738
01:00:27,361 --> 01:00:29,645
- Grandpa.
- Don't call me that!

739
01:00:33,741 --> 01:00:35,512
I'm sorry for worrying you.

740
01:00:36,635 --> 01:00:41,039
Hey. See these wrinkles?

741
01:00:41,465 --> 01:00:43,597
Every one of them is because of you.

742
01:00:43,907 --> 01:00:45,952
You ran off and put me through it.

743
01:00:46,241 --> 01:00:49,222
I'm sorry. I won't do it again.

744
01:00:49,901 --> 01:00:52,595
Forget it. I'm completely sulking.

745
01:00:52,707 --> 01:00:54,863
Please don't hate me too much.

746
01:00:58,410 --> 01:01:02,695
Hey, put yourself in my shoes.

747
01:01:02,961 --> 01:01:05,434
If you were me,
wouldn't you hate yourself?

748
01:01:05,635 --> 01:01:07,665
Anyone who makes my child cry...

749
01:01:11,771 --> 01:01:17,322
Never mind.
Just don't make your mother cry.

750
01:01:17,361 --> 01:01:21,120
Hey, anyone who makes your mother cry
is already waiting in line.

751
01:01:21,254 --> 01:01:22,382
Okay.

752
01:01:29,129 --> 01:01:30,231
Come here.

753
01:01:35,801 --> 01:01:40,138
So you don't hate me anymore?

754
01:01:41,635 --> 01:01:44,015
Hate you, but here we go again.

755
01:02:02,395 --> 01:02:07,320
Thanks to you, I had the happiest dream.

756
01:02:09,915 --> 01:02:12,040
I told everyone not to wake me,

757
01:02:12,101 --> 01:02:15,546
that I'd come after anyone who did,

758
01:02:17,622 --> 01:02:19,975
and I kept my claws out the whole time.

759
01:02:25,374 --> 01:02:27,021
Let's stop here.

760
01:02:31,568 --> 01:02:32,915
Gyu Rim.

761
01:02:35,134 --> 01:02:41,069
Even for the whole world,
I wouldn't trade...

762
01:02:43,081 --> 01:02:44,632
yesterday and today.

763
01:02:53,382 --> 01:02:57,545
Was my heart not enough?

764
01:03:00,955 --> 01:03:02,910
I was happy enough,

765
01:03:05,195 --> 01:03:07,180
more than grateful,

766
01:03:10,020 --> 01:03:14,109
so happy it brought tears.

767
01:03:16,474 --> 01:03:17,781
Then why?

768
01:03:19,901 --> 01:03:21,948
If we start again,

769
01:03:23,521 --> 01:03:27,627
someone is going to get hurt again.

770
01:03:29,482 --> 01:03:34,251
I don't want anyone getting hurt.

771
01:03:35,420 --> 01:03:37,478
Not me, not you, not anyone.

772
01:03:41,621 --> 01:03:46,966
They say you don't walk a road
whose end you can see.

773
01:03:49,721 --> 01:03:51,967
I couldn't have gone all the way anyway,

774
01:03:53,072 --> 01:03:56,558
and as a coward
without even that much courage,

775
01:03:58,575 --> 01:04:01,113
if I confused you and shook you,

776
01:04:02,894 --> 01:04:07,926
I'm so sorry for that too.

777
01:04:32,135 --> 01:04:34,029
I need to see the end of it, Gyu Rim.

778
01:04:41,001 --> 01:04:43,604
Even if I get hurt and you get hurt,

779
01:04:43,895 --> 01:04:46,029
even if someone else gets a little hurt,

780
01:04:46,852 --> 01:04:52,166
I have to see where we end up.

781
01:04:58,027 --> 01:04:59,418
I'm sorry, Gyu Rim.

782
01:05:30,544 --> 01:05:32,671
(Love on the Menu)

783
01:05:32,696 --> 01:05:34,177
I know that face from somewhere.

784
01:05:34,202 --> 01:05:35,821
- It's been a while, sir.
- Sir?

785
01:05:35,846 --> 01:05:38,186
Are you seeing my Gyu Rim again
or something?

786
01:05:38,211 --> 01:05:40,411
How much do you know about my brother?

787
01:05:40,554 --> 01:05:42,141
How much am I supposed to know?

788
01:05:42,166 --> 01:05:43,601
I'm not interested in the before.

789
01:05:43,626 --> 01:05:45,101
What in the world is all this?

790
01:05:45,126 --> 01:05:49,161
This lunchbox looks exactly like the ones
my mother used to pack for me.

791
01:05:49,186 --> 01:05:50,326
Take it back.

792
01:05:50,415 --> 01:05:52,136
I'm taking back what I said
about you seeing Gyu Rim again.

793
01:05:52,207 --> 01:05:53,449
We can't. We really can't.

794
01:05:53,474 --> 01:05:54,788
You're the only one I have.

795
01:05:54,909 --> 01:05:56,735
If it's not you, I don't want anyone else.

796
01:05:56,806 --> 01:05:57,941
I'm a single mother.

797
01:05:58,015 --> 01:05:59,785
That's solved if you marry me.

798
01:06:00,502 --> 01:06:02,302
Dramaday.me
